WEBVTT

00:14.200 --> 00:16.560
Hello, Fujiwara no Teika here.

00:16.560 --> 00:19.090
Good day, this is Ki no Tsurayuki.

00:19.090 --> 00:21.190
Say, Tsurayuki-senpai.

00:21.190 --> 00:22.450
Yes, Teika?

00:22.950 --> 00:26.520
The poets you introduced in
the preface to Kokin Wakashu

00:26.520 --> 00:28.880
became known as the Six Poetic Geniuses.

00:28.880 --> 00:30.190
Yes.

00:28.880 --> 00:38.340
The Six Poetic Geniuses
The Monk Henjo, Ariwara no Narihira, Funya no Yasuhide,
The Monk Kisen, Ono no Komachi, Otomo no Kuronushi

00:30.190 --> 00:33.110
The Monk Henjo, Ariwara no Narihira,

00:33.110 --> 00:35.680
Funya no Yasuhide, the Monk Kisen,

00:35.680 --> 00:38.350
Ono no Komachi, Otomo no Kuronushi.

00:38.680 --> 00:40.690
They were all wonderful poets.

00:40.690 --> 00:44.570
But you never said anything
complimentary about them.

00:44.570 --> 00:46.100
What? Really?

00:46.100 --> 00:49.190
In the case of Henjo,
Yoshimine no Munesada-sama,

00:49.190 --> 00:52.700
you described his poetry as
"structured and pretty,

00:52.700 --> 00:55.840
but as realistic as a 2D girl."

00:57.100 --> 01:00.530
Narihira was "passionate,
but not very eloquent.

01:00.530 --> 01:03.380
Reading his poetry was like
sniffing dead flowers."

01:03.380 --> 01:04.960
And your point is?

01:04.960 --> 01:07.920
Komachi's poems were "lovely, but timid.

01:07.920 --> 01:11.020
Like an ill person wearing thick makeup."

01:11.020 --> 01:11.800
What?!

01:12.310 --> 01:13.720
Things like that.

01:13.720 --> 01:16.240
Yep, those were all compliments.

01:16.240 --> 01:17.730
No, they weren't.

01:17.730 --> 01:19.380
Those were insults.

01:19.380 --> 01:20.800
Really?

01:20.800 --> 01:26.000
And you criticize them as if you think
they know nothing about poetry.

01:26.000 --> 01:28.520
I never thought I'd hear you say that.

01:28.520 --> 01:29.260
Huh?

01:29.260 --> 01:33.350
You chose five of the Six Poetic
Geniuses for the Hyakunin Isshu,

01:33.350 --> 01:36.320
but you didn't select Otomo no Kuronushi.

01:36.320 --> 01:37.160
Why not?

01:37.160 --> 01:39.630
Hmm, no real reason...

01:39.630 --> 01:42.110
He must feel very left out.

01:42.560 --> 01:43.650
Yes, that's right.

01:45.360 --> 01:48.750
Why was I the only one left out?

01:48.750 --> 01:50.820
Whoa! Kuronushi-dono!

01:50.820 --> 01:53.740
It's not nice to shun people.

01:53.740 --> 01:55.760
W-Wait, Kuronushi-dono.

01:55.760 --> 01:57.300
I didn't do that.

01:57.300 --> 01:58.720
Hey!  That's not fair!

01:58.720 --> 02:01.630
You're the one who said that
Kuronushi "had no class."

02:01.630 --> 02:04.380
We're talking about your
Hyakunin Isshu right now!

02:04.380 --> 02:05.480
Forget it.

02:05.480 --> 02:06.100
Huh?

02:06.770 --> 02:09.060
After all...  After all...

02:09.060 --> 02:11.480
I'm nothing more than...

02:11.480 --> 02:12.980
What?!

03:44.940 --> 03:47.280
Komachi-sama, you have a letter.

03:47.630 --> 03:48.760
Who is it from?

03:49.310 --> 03:51.710
Ariwara no Narihira-sama.

03:51.710 --> 03:52.710
Again?

03:53.310 --> 03:56.460
He keeps sending letters.
He just never gives up.

03:56.890 --> 03:59.300
You should stop accepting them.

03:59.300 --> 04:02.580
But it's a letter from
Ariwara no Narihira-sama.

04:02.580 --> 04:04.660
I could never refuse him.

04:09.020 --> 04:12.150
Dear brother, how are you doing?

04:12.670 --> 04:17.280
I would like to say that
I am as well as always,

04:17.280 --> 04:20.050
but there is a slight problem.

04:20.050 --> 04:24.780
Lately, Ariwara no Narihira-sama
has sent numerous letters

04:24.780 --> 04:27.770
with invitations such as,
"Let us gaze at the moon together."

04:28.240 --> 04:30.930
What should I do, dear brother?

04:31.650 --> 04:32.650
Yoshiko...

04:33.560 --> 04:35.310
I hear that you've made a name

04:35.310 --> 04:37.160
for yourself as Ono no Komachi,

04:37.160 --> 04:39.500
but you still come to me for help.

04:40.700 --> 04:44.070
But how unfortunate that
you've caught the eye of

04:44.070 --> 04:45.180
a nuisance like Narihira.

04:45.750 --> 04:48.540
I hear that he's approached
the Emperor's wives,

04:48.540 --> 04:50.780
and even the sacred Ise priestesses.

04:54.300 --> 04:57.440
Respond that you'll accept,
if he brings a friend.

04:58.020 --> 05:02.190
Narihira doesn't have any close
friends he could invite.

05:02.740 --> 05:05.740
Yasuhide and Narihira

05:02.740 --> 05:05.740
Funya no Yasuhide

05:07.610 --> 05:12.470
The grass and trees may change hue,

05:12.470 --> 05:15.710
yet autumn never comes
for the ocean blossoms.

05:17.060 --> 05:19.380
You expressed ocean waves as flowers?

05:19.840 --> 05:23.750
Indeed, waves don't change
colors like autumn leaves, but...

05:23.750 --> 05:27.040
An odd poem to recite at
a celebration of autumn.

05:27.040 --> 05:28.750
I thought I could sneak this by

05:28.750 --> 05:30.260
while nobody was paying attention.

05:30.940 --> 05:33.520
A poem without autumn doesn't
capture the desired essence.

05:33.520 --> 05:36.210
I believe that this poem is very
appropriate for Yasuhide-dono.

05:36.750 --> 05:40.540
Munesada-dono, you should not
praise this ornery poem.

05:40.540 --> 05:41.430
You think so?

05:43.280 --> 05:46.480
Could you give us a poem
without autumn, Kuronushi-dono?

05:46.480 --> 05:47.250
Huh?

05:47.250 --> 05:48.570
Uh...

05:48.570 --> 05:50.660
Without autumn...

05:50.660 --> 05:52.890
Mind if I give it a try?

05:53.920 --> 05:56.880
Oh, did you think of one, Narihira-dono?

05:56.880 --> 06:00.460
Yes, thanks to the lovely
chrysanthemums over there.

06:00.950 --> 06:03.590
Oh, I planted those last year.

06:03.980 --> 06:06.720
Then this poem will
be for Munesada-dono.

06:04.320 --> 06:06.720
A poem about chrysanthemums
without autumn?

06:08.010 --> 06:12.590
Can a chrysanthemum
bloom without autumn?

06:13.230 --> 06:16.300
Will the root die after
the petals have withered?

06:19.080 --> 06:20.590
The chrysanthemums will not bloom,

06:20.590 --> 06:22.690
if autumn doesn't come that year?

06:23.350 --> 06:26.640
Autumn comes every year,
so they will bloom every year.

06:26.640 --> 06:29.910
The petals may wither,
but the root will not die.

06:30.570 --> 06:33.560
As long as you care for your flowers...

06:34.190 --> 06:35.620
It's a good poem.

06:35.620 --> 06:37.400
A really good poem!

06:37.400 --> 06:39.260
I can't see the chrysanthemums
through my tears.

06:39.260 --> 06:41.670
You can never be without autumn.

06:42.450 --> 06:44.000
That was a clever twist.

06:44.520 --> 06:46.840
Well done, Narihira-dono.

06:46.840 --> 06:48.500
Allow me to pour you a cup.

06:48.500 --> 06:49.510
Thank you.

06:50.860 --> 06:52.820
By the way, Munesada-dono.

06:52.820 --> 06:54.390
Would you care to join me in gazing

06:54.390 --> 06:55.790
at the moon in the near future?

06:56.290 --> 06:59.240
Unfortunately, I'm completely booked.

06:59.710 --> 07:00.850
That's a pity.

07:01.300 --> 07:05.360
Damn, he made fun of me,
then he stole my thunder.

07:06.310 --> 07:09.260
The esteemed minister,
Ariwara no Narihira.

07:09.260 --> 07:12.280
He has pedigree, looks, and
he's also an excellent poet.

07:12.630 --> 07:14.380
I have a hard time believing
that he's human.

07:16.520 --> 07:18.880
Life is unfair.

07:18.880 --> 07:21.340
The people in higher positions
aren't particularly

07:21.340 --> 07:23.360
smarter than I am.

07:23.850 --> 07:28.020
It all depends on the family
you were born into.

07:28.940 --> 07:30.340
How absurd.

07:38.910 --> 07:42.100
Did he just shoot me a
really condescending look?!

07:42.340 --> 07:43.480
The bastard!

07:43.930 --> 07:44.560
Hey,

07:45.300 --> 07:47.650
he seems upset with you.

07:47.650 --> 07:49.410
I'm the one who's upset with him!

07:49.410 --> 07:51.300
He's making me look like a fool!

07:50.180 --> 07:52.820
No, I'm referring to the last Imperial visit.

07:53.030 --> 07:54.540
Damn those bums who only

07:54.540 --> 07:56.480
land in high positions
because of their parents.

07:56.480 --> 07:58.950
This country is falling
apart because we're led

07:58.950 --> 08:00.620
by people who have never
had to spend effort.

08:00.620 --> 08:02.590
I think he heard you.

08:02.590 --> 08:03.710
Seriously?!

08:04.100 --> 08:06.230
He's got sharp ears.

08:06.230 --> 08:08.170
Your voice is too loud.

08:08.170 --> 08:09.770
This is bad...

08:09.770 --> 08:12.130
My chances for promotion
were already slim,

08:12.130 --> 08:14.340
but now I've antagonized
someone in power!

08:18.080 --> 08:19.300
Narihira-dono!

08:20.420 --> 08:23.640
I apologize for my previous behavior!

08:23.640 --> 08:25.030
What's he doing?

08:25.030 --> 08:27.100
I've never seen someone
prostrating himself before.

08:27.100 --> 08:27.910
What do you mean?

08:27.910 --> 08:29.610
During the Imperial visit!

08:29.890 --> 08:34.570
I spoke ill of you because
my heart was too weak!

08:33.540 --> 08:36.880
Heheh, he'll have to forgive me

08:34.570 --> 08:36.880
I was so frustrated with
my own shortcomings

08:36.880 --> 08:38.450
after I've apologized in front of witnesses.

08:36.880 --> 08:39.300
that I used you as a scapegoat!

08:39.400 --> 08:40.460
Is this a calculated move?

08:41.920 --> 08:45.210
I'll look like a bad guy
if I don't forgive you.

08:45.210 --> 08:46.080
Stop it.

08:46.080 --> 08:48.000
No, I must speak my mind!

08:48.300 --> 08:50.140
My nasty nature is to blame!

08:49.330 --> 08:51.880
Damn, I'll just have to kiss his ass.

08:50.140 --> 08:51.880
I couldn't help but feel jealous when

08:51.880 --> 08:53.490
He's just another spoiled rich kid.

08:51.880 --> 08:56.790
I saw you riding on that
horse with such grace.

08:53.490 --> 08:55.260
I can win him over by sucking up.

08:56.790 --> 08:58.380
You talk a lot.

08:59.130 --> 09:01.590
I don't plan on moving up the ladder.

09:01.590 --> 09:03.210
Currying my favor won't do you any good.

09:03.530 --> 09:04.180
Huh?

09:04.540 --> 09:07.220
I don't like people who
flaunt their rank,

09:07.220 --> 09:10.190
and I don't like people
who cower before rank.

09:10.190 --> 09:13.330
Did you think the poem I wrote
that beat yours yesterday

09:13.330 --> 09:15.810
was meant as payback for your insult?

09:15.810 --> 09:17.040
Huh?  No...

09:17.040 --> 09:19.150
No need to worry then.

09:19.150 --> 09:22.180
I'm used to having the
unskilled lash out at me.

09:22.180 --> 09:22.830
Unskilled?

09:23.320 --> 09:24.670
I just wanted to

09:24.670 --> 09:28.130
show you up yesterday because
I heard you were a fine poet.

09:28.620 --> 09:30.030
Did I confuse you?

09:30.030 --> 09:31.290
So sorry about that.

09:31.290 --> 09:33.540
You got on your knees for nothing.

09:35.090 --> 09:38.590
No, my apology served its purpose.

09:38.590 --> 09:41.220
Really?  That's nice.

09:41.220 --> 09:43.360
I think we can be friends.

09:43.360 --> 09:44.020
Huh?

09:44.520 --> 09:46.480
Now, my friend.

09:46.480 --> 09:48.630
I want you to come hunting with me.

09:48.630 --> 09:49.360
What?

09:50.030 --> 09:52.540
Right now?  The sun's about to set.

09:52.540 --> 09:54.690
I'm not very skilled with a bow...

09:54.690 --> 09:57.370
Doesn't matter.
As long as you can recite poetry.

09:58.070 --> 09:59.060
Poetry?

10:03.590 --> 10:07.680
Uh, were you talking
about hunting women?

10:07.680 --> 10:09.100
That's one way to look at it.

10:09.100 --> 10:11.820
Let's see who can win her
over with poetry first.

10:11.820 --> 10:12.500
Huh?!

10:12.890 --> 10:15.250
Hey, keep it down.

10:15.250 --> 10:17.120
They'll find us.

10:17.120 --> 10:19.190
I'm not going to compete with you!

10:19.190 --> 10:21.060
Stop joking around!

10:21.060 --> 10:23.010
Oh?  You don't feel up to the task?

10:23.480 --> 10:25.510
If you claim to be an excellent poet,

10:25.510 --> 10:27.390
you must be well versed in love poems.

10:27.810 --> 10:29.340
Absolutely not!

10:29.340 --> 10:31.110
My poems are meant for entertainment!

10:31.110 --> 10:32.400
I don't know how to write love poems!

10:33.000 --> 10:35.990
This woman happens to be a famous poet,

10:35.990 --> 10:39.020
so she might take a fancy to your poems.

10:39.020 --> 10:42.370
Huh?  Who lives here?

10:42.790 --> 10:45.520
Are you familiar with Ono no Komachi?

10:45.520 --> 10:48.730
The most beautiful member
of the Imperial Harem

10:48.730 --> 10:50.240
who is a favorite of the Emperor?

10:51.100 --> 10:52.560
Y-You can't mean to say...

10:52.560 --> 10:55.240
Yes, this is Komachi's villa.

10:55.730 --> 10:57.630
I hear she's currently on
leave from the palace.

10:58.480 --> 11:00.800
I'm not going to ignore
this opportunity.

11:00.800 --> 11:03.760
You're making a move on
the Emperor's favorite?!

11:04.650 --> 11:06.240
Your voice is too loud.

11:06.820 --> 11:07.720
Who's there?!

11:09.020 --> 11:10.430
Welcome.

11:12.080 --> 11:14.230
I apologize for the rude welcome.

11:14.230 --> 11:16.450
No, we should be apologizing.

11:16.450 --> 11:19.270
Forgive us for disturbing
you on this quiet night.

11:20.480 --> 11:21.970
I'm finished...

11:20.480 --> 11:23.820
I didn't expect you to come visit me.

11:21.970 --> 11:23.820
My life is finished...

11:24.320 --> 11:26.230
You lied, dear brother!

11:24.320 --> 11:29.560
I never dreamed you would
grant me an audience so readily.

11:26.230 --> 11:28.170
Narihira-sama has friends!

11:29.590 --> 11:31.290
I didn't have much of a choice.

11:31.710 --> 11:33.720
Since I promised to join you in gazing

11:33.720 --> 11:36.100
at the moon, if you brought a friend.

11:36.870 --> 11:37.630
Huh?

11:38.250 --> 11:40.300
What's she talking about, Narihira-dono?

11:40.300 --> 11:41.390
I have no idea.

11:41.390 --> 11:43.850
Are you Funya no Yasuhide-sama?

11:43.850 --> 11:44.640
Y-Yes!

11:45.140 --> 11:46.960
I've heard many stories about you.

11:46.960 --> 11:48.050
Stories?

11:48.050 --> 11:51.390
They say that you're an expert on poetry,
a rare person in this age.

11:51.940 --> 11:54.020
I'm happy to meet you.

11:54.020 --> 11:56.530
Oh...  Yes...

11:57.440 --> 11:59.570
Tonight is the night after a full moon.

11:59.570 --> 12:01.850
It will be beautiful to behold.

12:07.770 --> 12:09.080
Well, gentlemen?

12:09.750 --> 12:12.960
How do you feel after
gazing at this moon?

12:13.230 --> 12:15.640
I'm feeling lonely as I
think of unrequited love

12:15.640 --> 12:18.920
and the heartless woman who got away.

12:19.270 --> 12:22.210
My, perhaps the moon detests you

12:22.210 --> 12:25.930
for only blaming me as heartless
and failing to catch me.

12:26.160 --> 12:27.490
Absolutely right.

12:27.490 --> 12:30.670
You are a fool for expecting
her to come eagerly.

12:30.670 --> 12:31.890
A luna-tic, if you will.

12:35.870 --> 12:38.540
Were you able to catch
the moon, Yasuhide-sama?

12:38.540 --> 12:42.070
No, she turns a blind eye to me,

12:42.750 --> 12:44.950
even when I wear my heart on my sleeve.

12:45.910 --> 12:47.370
More wordplay?

12:47.720 --> 12:50.260
I was born to be a joker.

12:50.700 --> 12:52.620
You talk too much.

12:53.020 --> 12:54.560
Haven't you had a little
too much to drink?

12:55.070 --> 12:57.320
It helps me perform better.

12:57.830 --> 12:59.420
I'm quite grateful.

13:00.180 --> 13:02.210
If Narihira-sama and I were alone,

13:02.210 --> 13:04.680
we would be seeing sparks fly.

13:05.080 --> 13:06.260
You are a life saver.

13:07.420 --> 13:08.620
You're welcome...

13:08.620 --> 13:10.540
That's harsh.

13:11.350 --> 13:15.060
I prefer a little tension
while gazing at the moon.

13:12.190 --> 13:15.310
The esteemed minister,
Ariwara no Narihira,

13:15.060 --> 13:18.650
Oh?  Wouldn't you lose interest if
the moon were to fall in your lap?

13:15.810 --> 13:18.650
the Emperor's favorite, Ono no Komachi,

13:18.650 --> 13:20.750
and me, a poor noble.

13:21.450 --> 13:23.350
What a peculiar gathering.

13:24.020 --> 13:28.150
Will I get in trouble for drinking
with the Emperor's favorite?

13:28.620 --> 13:29.850
Yasuhide-sama.

13:29.850 --> 13:30.530
Yes!

13:31.500 --> 13:33.530
Are you listening?

13:34.680 --> 13:36.320
I-I'm sorry!

13:35.410 --> 13:38.840
Komachi's a mean drunk.

13:36.220 --> 13:38.840
Are you too busy thinking
about someone else?

13:38.840 --> 13:40.880
No!  Er...

13:41.430 --> 13:46.550
I ask this question
of every poet I meet:

13:47.850 --> 13:51.930
Why did you choose to become a poet?

13:55.260 --> 13:57.190
My story isn't very interesting,

13:57.750 --> 14:00.420
but I always felt that
poetry was the only option

14:00.420 --> 14:02.820
for an untalented person, like myself.

14:03.270 --> 14:05.460
I wanted to become a scholar,

14:06.060 --> 14:07.880
but I had no sponsor,

14:07.880 --> 14:09.690
and my average intelligence

14:09.690 --> 14:12.790
was never enough as I
struggled to make ends meet.

14:12.790 --> 14:14.340
I had to make a decision.

14:14.980 --> 14:18.040
If I became a poet, I would be judged

14:18.040 --> 14:20.920
on my ability, not my background.

14:22.600 --> 14:24.950
Oh, I-I'm very sorry.

14:24.950 --> 14:26.360
That was a mundane story.

14:26.360 --> 14:28.220
No, not at all.

14:28.590 --> 14:30.760
It provided some fascinating insight.

14:30.760 --> 14:32.180
Isn't that right, Narihira-sama?

14:32.640 --> 14:33.640
I suppose.

14:34.980 --> 14:36.260
Really...

14:36.720 --> 14:38.410
I'm not sure if I should feel happy

14:38.410 --> 14:39.770
that the rich and famous understand.

14:40.830 --> 14:43.260
Life is a drag.

14:43.260 --> 14:45.480
Social status makes all the difference.

14:45.480 --> 14:47.670
You and I may be separated
by our status,

14:48.640 --> 14:51.440
but neither of us can escape
our responsibilities.

14:52.040 --> 14:54.460
Living in such a confining society,

14:54.460 --> 14:57.200
I often feel as though I will lose my identity.

14:57.920 --> 14:59.610
I didn't want that.

14:59.610 --> 15:02.940
I wanted to be myself,
to express myself...

15:04.110 --> 15:09.000
Poetry is our way of seeking freedom.

15:14.350 --> 15:15.430
I see...

15:16.020 --> 15:17.650
So I wasn't the only one.

15:19.170 --> 15:22.510
I chose poetry because it
is free of social status,

15:22.510 --> 15:26.270
while they chose poetry
for other freedoms.

15:28.180 --> 15:32.060
The moon is so lovely tonight.

15:32.060 --> 15:35.360
The moon's beauty pales
in comparison to yours.

15:36.150 --> 15:40.500
Narihira-sama, you're exactly
as everyone says you are.

15:41.010 --> 15:43.530
I must say that I enjoy
spending the night

15:43.530 --> 15:47.260
free of obligation while talking
about the moon and poetry.

15:52.350 --> 15:54.970
Still, something about this
doesn't feel right.

15:55.300 --> 15:58.580
I didn't get to hear you
recite a love poem.

15:58.580 --> 16:00.840
I was really looking forward to that.

16:01.450 --> 16:05.900
I'm honored to hear you say that,
but could you tone it down?

16:06.450 --> 16:09.570
I was expecting to be exiled
when we were caught.

16:10.600 --> 16:12.040
You're a coward.

16:12.040 --> 16:13.920
That explains why you
can't do love poems.

16:14.580 --> 16:16.430
Your poems will never be
more than entertainment,

16:16.430 --> 16:18.120
if you worry about others' opinions.

16:18.120 --> 16:20.370
If there's a woman you want,
let those feelings out.

16:20.370 --> 16:23.000
Don't spend too much time
on the technical side.

16:23.670 --> 16:25.580
You need to liberate yourself.

16:25.580 --> 16:29.380
Poetry will come naturally,
when you unleash your emotions.

16:31.680 --> 16:36.080
I envy your naivety.

16:37.190 --> 16:40.130
You can only say these things
because of the position you're in.

16:40.820 --> 16:42.870
A man from the borderlands, like myself,

16:42.870 --> 16:45.520
can only survive by paying attention
to what other people think.

16:46.160 --> 16:47.700
I don't have the ability to come up

16:47.700 --> 16:50.150
with poems on the spot, as you do.

16:50.750 --> 16:52.280
You may say that it would be

16:52.280 --> 16:54.800
boorish to get involved
in power struggles,

16:54.800 --> 16:57.790
but I hope you realize that you're free

16:57.790 --> 17:01.710
to write poetry because
of your social status.

17:02.730 --> 17:04.040
What's your point?

17:04.750 --> 17:07.750
Am I supposed to act like
a servant, the way you do?

17:07.750 --> 17:10.090
That wasn't my point.

17:10.090 --> 17:11.090
I'm...

17:12.000 --> 17:13.730
Sorry, but I'm leaving.

17:14.810 --> 17:17.820
I left the mountains to escape the wind,

17:17.820 --> 17:20.460
and instead, I get a lecture.

17:20.460 --> 17:22.260
P-Please wait!

17:23.960 --> 17:25.290
Gust of wind!

17:27.160 --> 17:31.640
Gust of wind carries leaves from the trees,

17:32.300 --> 17:36.050
giving the name of storm to the mountain wind.

17:37.250 --> 17:39.440
Look!  The autumn wind's so
strong in the mountains

17:39.440 --> 17:41.030
that leaves are falling off the trees!

17:41.030 --> 17:44.060
Is that why the mountain
wind is called a storm?

17:41.780 --> 17:44.620
Mountain Wind

17:41.780 --> 17:44.620
"Storm"

17:47.390 --> 17:52.700
What are you trying to say
with all this wordplay?

17:53.170 --> 17:54.630
Nothing important.

17:54.630 --> 17:56.470
I'm just trying to sound clever.

17:56.470 --> 17:57.970
Worthless.

17:57.970 --> 18:00.410
I could never come up with
a poem with no point.

18:00.410 --> 18:01.770
Yes, that's right.

18:02.780 --> 18:05.100
I am the only one who could
think of such a poem.

18:05.740 --> 18:09.470
Narihira-dono, you have amazing ability.

18:09.980 --> 18:12.430
Plus, you've been blessed with
the ideal environment.

18:13.130 --> 18:15.440
I want you to understand
how fortunate you are.

18:16.020 --> 18:19.780
Then you can compose many poems of joy.

18:20.440 --> 18:23.200
You are the only one who can do that.

18:23.720 --> 18:26.800
Likewise, there are
poems only I can compose

18:26.800 --> 18:28.980
with my unfortunate background.

18:29.460 --> 18:32.350
Poems that no one else can ever imitate.

18:33.170 --> 18:34.880
They are my identity.

18:35.520 --> 18:37.180
As long as I remember that,

18:37.180 --> 18:38.950
I will never be buried by responsibility.

18:39.590 --> 18:42.910
That is how poetry sets me free.

18:44.180 --> 18:48.030
Well, I just realized all of that now.

18:49.540 --> 18:54.860
Narihira-dono, it was pathetic
of me to speak ill of you.

18:55.270 --> 18:56.370
Please forgive me.

18:56.930 --> 18:59.030
While our poetry may be different,

18:59.430 --> 19:03.490
I would like to share my poems
with you in the future.

19:04.200 --> 19:06.230
That was the plan.

19:06.230 --> 19:07.000
Huh?

19:08.160 --> 19:10.440
Your poetry sets you free?

19:10.440 --> 19:12.830
You're just showing off your technique.

19:12.830 --> 19:15.230
Well, that's the selling point...

19:15.230 --> 19:16.550
Makes sense.

19:16.990 --> 19:19.550
I could never imitate your style.

19:24.050 --> 19:26.410
Let's have another contest,
when you have time.

19:26.860 --> 19:28.580
I won't lose next time.

19:28.580 --> 19:30.920
I have a special pun prepared.

19:30.920 --> 19:33.440
If I lose to a pun,
I'll swallow my pen.

19:39.180 --> 19:42.810
Koma-chi   Nari-pi   Ya-sun

19:39.940 --> 19:42.330
Ya-sun!  Nari-pi!  Koma-chi!

19:42.820 --> 19:45.780
One day...

19:47.000 --> 19:47.830
Yasuhide?

19:47.830 --> 19:49.740
Oh, Narihira-dono.

19:49.740 --> 19:51.350
Why do you have a runny nose?

19:52.030 --> 19:54.470
It was a little chilly last night.

19:54.470 --> 19:55.750
You should have started the fires.

19:55.750 --> 19:57.800
Well, we need to conserve firewood

19:57.800 --> 19:59.620
or we won't have enough
to last until spring.

19:59.620 --> 20:00.660
I see.

20:00.660 --> 20:02.450
The life of a poor
noble sounds difficult.

20:03.710 --> 20:05.100
It's okay when I say it,

20:05.100 --> 20:07.250
but when someone else says it, I get mad!

20:07.250 --> 20:09.150
Try not to infect anyone in the palace.

20:09.150 --> 20:10.860
I don't want anyone inheriting
your horrible pun sense.

20:10.860 --> 20:13.350
You're not going to worry about me!

20:13.350 --> 20:15.480
Oh, Yasuhide-sama is ill?

20:15.860 --> 20:18.900
He's dripping snot all over the palace.
It's quite unattractive.

20:18.900 --> 20:20.460
The poor man.

20:20.460 --> 20:22.310
You don't need to worry about him.

20:22.790 --> 20:23.840
Anyway...

20:24.910 --> 20:26.550
What's that in your hand?

20:26.550 --> 20:28.370
Oh, this is a tachibana.

20:30.340 --> 20:31.830
What is this?

20:31.830 --> 20:34.890
There was an artist who
drew a face for me.

20:34.890 --> 20:36.710
Doesn't it look just
like Yasuhide-sama?

20:37.190 --> 20:39.380
I also have one that looks
like you, Narihira-sama.

20:41.460 --> 20:43.250
Well?  Do you see the resemblance?

20:46.100 --> 20:47.680
Cold gets worse...

20:46.740 --> 20:48.000
Big Brother!

20:48.530 --> 20:50.660
Man, I can't get any rest...

20:50.660 --> 20:51.940
Big Brother,

20:52.620 --> 20:54.860
we received a big load of firewood.

20:54.860 --> 20:56.110
Oh, wow.

20:56.110 --> 20:57.680
Here's the letter.

20:59.440 --> 21:04.360
Stay warm and recover soon.
-Komachi

21:04.360 --> 21:05.240
Komachi...

21:05.570 --> 21:07.180
Is she a rich young lady?

21:07.180 --> 21:08.660
Do you have a shot?

21:08.660 --> 21:10.660
I want a rich sister-in-law!

21:10.660 --> 21:12.810
No, she's out of my reach,
in more ways than one.

21:12.810 --> 21:15.500
Oh, and here I was thinking
that you finally got lucky.

21:15.500 --> 21:16.800
That's lame, Big Brother.

21:16.800 --> 21:18.880
Oh, she even sent rice?

21:18.880 --> 21:20.690
I don't know how to thank her.

21:20.690 --> 21:22.310
No, that came separately.

21:22.310 --> 21:23.020
Separately?

21:23.020 --> 21:24.010
There was a man.

21:24.010 --> 21:26.090
He left without telling me his name.

21:29.370 --> 21:30.560
What is this?

21:37.230 --> 21:40.210
The ocean is so comforting.

21:43.440 --> 21:45.850
Sorry about breaking your watermelon.

21:45.850 --> 21:49.290
That's okay.  It was Tsurayuki-senpai's.

21:49.290 --> 21:52.530
Oh, then I should apologize.

21:54.120 --> 21:56.300
<i>History describes Otomo no Kuronushi-dono</i>

21:56.300 --> 21:59.440
<i>as an evil man who is
portrayed as a villain</i>

21:59.440 --> 22:02.050
<i>in Noh and Kabuki theater.</i>

22:02.840 --> 22:05.020
<i>At least part of the blame
probably goes to Tsurayuki-senpai's</i>

22:05.020 --> 22:07.660
<i>unflattering introduction and my decision</i>

22:07.660 --> 22:11.180
<i>to omit him from the Hyakunin Isshu.</i>

22:12.890 --> 22:14.090
Kuronushi-dono...

22:15.570 --> 22:18.600
Sorry about leaving you out.

22:20.730 --> 22:22.270
It's okay.

22:29.350 --> 22:31.280
This watermelon is good.

22:32.950 --> 22:34.950
Poetic Tale 4:

22:32.950 --> 22:34.950
END

24:04.960 --> 24:20.640
Next
Episode

24:04.960 --> 24:20.640
Eastward

24:04.960 --> 24:20.640
Ono no Komachi

24:06.800 --> 24:11.770
So the flower has wilted
during the long spring rains,

24:12.430 --> 24:14.400
just as my beauty has faded

24:14.400 --> 24:16.190
during my forlorn years in this world.
